"""Join verified metadata with deliberately bounded reading notes."""
import csv,html,json,pathlib
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];metadata=R/'research'/'metadata'
# key: workload; hardware; strategy; evidence; limitation/overlap. NR means not extracted, not absent from the paper.
notes={
'canny1986':('Canny; mathematical detector formulation','Not a CPU/GPU benchmark','Detection/localization criteria; gradient maxima and hysteresis','Foundational detector derivation; not a speedup source','Defines algorithm family; our discrete binomial variant is not the full multiscale formulation'),
'luo2008':('Canny; CUDA; OpenCV/MATLAB CPU baselines','GeForce 8800 GTX, 768 MB; CPU model not extracted','Full pipeline including connected-component hysteresis','Runtime across image resolutions; source full text inspected','Direct prior GPU Canny; output differences acknowledged by authors; not evidence for our exact variant'),
'emrani2017':('Sobel, Prewitt, Roberts and Canny; CUDA/OpenCV/MATLAB','Exact GPU model not extracted','Parallel alternative to BFS for Canny edge tracking','OCT images; execution-time comparisons','Direct multi-detector overlap; does not establish our particular row-partition benefit'),
'song2024':('Canny; sequential/OpenMP/CUDA/OpenCL','Intel i7-8700K and GTX 1050 discussed; multiple platforms','Task partition, vector access and NDRange tuning','Images and resolutions; runtime and acceleration metrics','Direct comparison overlap; local-neighbor threshold description warrants semantic caution versus global hysteresis'),
'chang2023':('Four-direction 5x5 Sobel; GPU','Jetson AGX Xavier and GTX 1650Ti','Warp primitives, prefetch and operator transformation','Kernel comparisons with OpenCV GPU','Different operator than our two-direction 3x3; hardware-specific gains cannot transfer directly'),
'mochurad2022':('Canny; CUDA','Not extracted from inspected abstract','Parallel algorithm; image noise/complexity analysis','Image-size and kernel-size speedups; noise sensitivity','Already studies resolution effects; not validation of our implementation or CPU/GPU partitions'),
'recent2026':('Canny pipeline; NumPy/SciPy and CuPy/CuPyX','Three heterogeneous environments; exact models not extracted','AppModel, OpModel, TransferModel; stage-aware latency SLO selection','Publisher abstract: prediction error and configuration selection evaluation','Strong recent overlap with performance-aware allocation; our study is simpler and not a novel stage-selection method'),
'qilin':('Eight computational benchmarks including image convolution; CPU/GPU','Multicore CPU and NVIDIA GPU; exact primary configuration not extracted','Adaptive runtime mapping from trained performance estimates','Manual/static/adaptive mappings; latency and energy; varying sizes','Direct precedent for throughput-informed partitioning; our fixed sweep is narrower'),
'skmd':('OpenCL data-parallel kernels','One multicore CPU and two asymmetric GPUs in reported evaluation','Automatic partition, partial kernels, output merge; transfer awareness','Real-hardware comparison against fastest-device strategy','Direct precedent for collaboration including transfers; our hand-coded row split is not a new runtime'),
'starpu':('Numerical tasks; heterogeneous runtime','Multicore CPU plus GPU; exact models not extracted','Dynamic task scheduling and data management','Runtime strategies and MAGMA comparison in publisher abstract','Task-runtime precedent; our single-image split does not replace StarPU'),
'hybrid2014':('CUDA kernels; CPU/GPU runtime','Exact models unavailable in inspected publisher abstract','Runtime distribution queue and transparent memory','GPU-only comparison reported in abstract','Automatic hybrid execution predates our project; no numerical comparison across systems'),
'survey2018':('Survey of cooperative CPU/GPU computing','Multiple studies; no single benchmark platform','Taxonomy of collaboration and allocation approaches','Publisher abstract and topic overview','Secondary synthesis for search guidance; not direct evidence for our measured speedup'),
'fluidic':('OpenCL cooperative execution','Not extracted','FluidiCL runtime; cooperative execution across devices','Metadata and author publication list verified; detailed full-text review pending','Relevant allocation precedent; no quantitative findings asserted'),
'rodinia':('Diverse heterogeneous kernels; OpenMP and CUDA','GTX 280 and 3.2 GHz quad-core Core 2 Extreme','Benchmark diversity and data-layout characterization','Performance, communication and power measurements','Motivates varied workloads; two edge algorithms cannot represent all heterogeneous programs'),
'roofline':('Multicore performance modeling','Multiple architectures; not extracted here','Operational intensity and attainable performance ceilings','Primary report and publisher-deposited metadata','Explanatory framework only; no roofline bottleneck claimed without counters/bandwidth measurements'),
'teodoro':('Large-scale image feature analyses; CPU/GPU','Parallel CPU/GPU system; exact devices not extracted','Performance-aware co-scheduling and pipeline optimizations','Official proceedings abstract: CPU-only/GPU-only/cooperative evaluation','Direct image-processing scheduling precedent; our per-image stencil experiment has narrower scope'),
'datta':('Nearest-neighbor stencils','Intel Clovertown, AMD Barcelona, Sun Victoria Falls, PowerXCell 8i, GTX280','Blocking, locality, SIMD and auto-tuning','Cross-architecture stencil measurements','Tiling is established and architecture-sensitive; this is not our measured roofline'),
'nickolls':('CUDA programming model','CUDA-capable manycore GPU architecture','Thread hierarchy, shared memory and synchronization','Programming-model exposition on NVIDIA research page','Foundational programming reference, not proof that our candidate optimization is faster'),
'halide':('Feed-forward image pipelines; ARM/x86/GPU','ARM/x86/GPU; exact models not extracted','Separate algorithm from schedule; tiling, fusion and recomputation','Author page describes application comparisons','Algorithm-preserving scheduling is established; we use handwritten loops rather than Halide'),
'measurementbias':('Systems performance evaluation','Pentium 4, Core 2 and m5 O3CPU; GCC/Intel compiler','Causal analysis and setup randomization','IBM author abstract; SPEC CPU2006 measurement bias','Random configuration order helps but does not eliminate laptop thermal/system bias'),
'georges':('Java performance evaluation methodology','Java platforms; not a CUDA benchmark','Repeated measurement and rigorous statistical analysis','Author paper and institutional bibliographic record','Methodological context only; our short within-process samples are not independent cross-session replications')}
manual={
'qilin':dict(title='Qilin: Exploiting Parallelism on Heterogeneous Multiprocessors with Adaptive Mapping',author='Chi-Keung Luk; Sunpyo Hong; Hyesoon Kim',year=2009,venue='MICRO',url='https://faculty.cc.gatech.edu/~hyesoon/qilin_luk.pdf'),
'halide':dict(title='Decoupling Algorithms from Schedules for Easy Optimization of Image Processing Pipelines',author='Jonathan Ragan-Kelley; Andrew Adams; Sylvain Paris; Marc Levoy; Saman Amarasinghe; Fredo Durand',year=2012,venue='ACM Transactions on Graphics 31(4)',url='https://people.csail.mit.edu/jrk/halide12/')}
rows=[]
for key,values in notes.items():
 if key in manual:row={'key':key,**manual[key],'doi':''}
 else:
  m=json.loads((metadata/(key+'.json')).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))['message'];row=dict(key=key,title=html.unescape(m['title'][0])+(': '+m['subtitle'][0] if m.get('subtitle') else ''),author='; '.join((a.get('given','')+' '+a.get('family','')).strip() for a in m.get('author',[])),year=m.get('published-print',m.get('published',m['issued']))['date-parts'][0][0],venue=html.unescape(m.get('container-title',[''])[0]),url=m['URL'],doi=m['DOI'])
 row.update(zip(['algorithm_model','hardware','strategy','evaluation_findings','limitations_overlap'],values));row['difference']='Reproducible single-laptop characterization with exact Sobel equivalence; no claim of algorithmic novelty';rows.append(row)
with (R/'research'/'related_work_matrix.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
 writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(rows[0]));writer.writeheader();writer.writerows(rows)
intro='''# Literature review\n\nStatus: NEEDS REVIEW for submission-level completeness; 21 research publications selected, plus technical documentation. Search date: 2026-10-26. This is a focused narrative review, not a systematic-review claim. Primary publisher pages, author-hosted papers, official proceedings, and Crossref deposits were checked. Full-text depth differs by record; absent hardware fields mean not extracted, never invented. Bibliographic existence is distinct from replicating or endorsing a paper's conclusions.\n\n## Search and selection\n\nQueries covered CUDA/OpenMP Sobel, CUDA Canny, cooperative image processing, adaptive mapping, transfer-aware scheduling, stencil tiling and measurement bias. Qilin, SKMD, StarPU and the 2026 stage-aware Canny paper are especially consequential to novelty. Citation chaining from the 2024 PLOS paper identified earlier hybrid and CUDA Canny work. Excluded unverified promotional claims, unrelated edge-device DNN papers, and unrelated conferences sharing acronyms. No claimed literature speedup is used as our experimental data.\n\n## Synthesis\n\nGPU Canny is established, including complete hysteresis handling in Luo and Duraiswami and alternatives to BFS in Emrani et al. Song et al. directly compare CPU, OpenMP, CUDA and OpenCL. Their described local-neighbor threshold step should not be assumed equivalent to unrestricted global edge tracking. Chang et al. study a different, four-direction 5x5 Sobel operator; their optimized kernel cannot be treated as an apples-to-apples baseline for our 3x3 L1 operator.\n\nCPU/GPU cooperation and transfer-aware partitioning have long precedents in Qilin, SKMD, StarPU, FluidiCL, and performance-aware image-analysis scheduling. Huang et al. (2026) further provide stage-aware Canny allocation with transfer-aware prediction. A generic rate-ratio formula or row split is therefore not novel. Our defensible contribution is a transparent, bounded replication/characterization on a particular laptop, with raw observations and identical Sobel outputs.\n\nDatta et al. and Halide motivate separating algorithm semantics from schedule choices. Roofline offers explanatory concepts, but absent hardware-counter measurements we cannot establish a bandwidth-bound diagnosis. Rodinia motivates workload diversity; our synthetic corpus and two algorithms remain much narrower. Measurement-bias and repeated-evaluation literature justify reporting spread and avoiding significance claims from a single session.\n\n## Reading records\n\n'''
for row in rows:
 intro+=f"### {row['key']}: {row['title']}\n\n{row['author']}. {row['venue']}, {row['year']}. [Primary/DOI source]({row['url']}).\n\n"
 for label,k in [('Workload/programming model','algorithm_model'),('Hardware','hardware'),('Strategy','strategy'),('Evidence and findings','evaluation_findings'),('Limits and overlap','limitations_overlap')]:intro+=f"- {label}: {row[k]}.\n"
 intro+='\n'
(R/'research'/'literature_review.md').write_text(intro,encoding='utf-8')
bib=(R/'research'/'crossref.bib').read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('Yuancheng Luo,  and','Luo, Yuancheng and').replace(r'\&amp;',r'\&')
bib+=(R/'research'/'manual.bib').read_text(encoding='utf-8');(R/'research'/'references.bib').write_text(bib,encoding='utf-8')
if (R/'paper').exists():(R/'paper'/'references.bib').write_text(bib,encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote',len(rows),'review records; bibliography includes 2 technical documents.')
